---
description: Manage Flutter form state with variables; avoid TextEditingController unless required
alwaysApply: true
---

# Flutter Form State

Default to local variables updated through `onChanged` or `onSubmitted`. Do not create a `TextEditingController` unless programmatic text manipulation is explicitly required.

## Default: variables + callbacks

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
class LoginForm extends StatefulWidget { ... }

class _LoginFormState extends State<LoginForm> {
  String _email = '';

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return TextField(
      onChanged: (value) => setState(() => _email = value),
      onSubmitted: (_) => _submit(),
    );
  }
}
```

```dart
// ❌ BAD — controller with no programmatic text edits
final _emailController = TextEditingController();

TextField(controller: _emailController)
```

## When a controller is required

Use `TextEditingController` only when the field text must be set, cleared, or selected from code (e.g. `text`, `selection`, `clear()`).

Dispose it in `dispose()`:

```dart
// ✅ GOOD — required controller, disposed
class _SearchFieldState extends State<SearchField> {
  final _controller = TextEditingController();

  @override
  void dispose() {
    _controller.dispose();
    super.dispose();
  }
}
```

```dart
// ❌ BAD — controller never disposed
final _controller = TextEditingController();
```
